# 9. MANUAL SETTINGS EDIT → OUTDATED KNOWLEDGE

This is a core Round 3.3 requirement.

Example:

Previously approved document:

```text
Consultation = GHS 500
```

Settings synchronized:

```text
Consultation = GHS 500
```

Later the owner manually changes Settings:

```text
Consultation = GHS 550
```

The manual Settings change is an explicit authenticated human action.

Therefore:

```text
GHS 550 = authoritative current Settings
```

The old document-linked fact must become:

```text
OUTDATED
aiUsable = false
```

The related document should receive an:

```text
OUTDATED
```

governance condition/status where appropriate.

Reason:

```text
SETTINGS_CHANGED_AFTER_APPROVAL
```

---

# 10. OUTDATED IS DIFFERENT FROM CONFLICT

These two scenarios must behave differently.

## Unresolved uploaded-document conflict

```text
Settings = 400
New document = 500
Human has not reviewed
```

Runtime:

```text
Neither disputed value should be confidently used.
Human handoff if customer needs it.
```

## Manual Settings update after previous approval

```text
Approved document = 500
Owner manually changes Settings = 550
```

Runtime:

```text
Settings 550 is authoritative.
Old document fact becomes OUTDATED.
AI may use 550.
```

This distinction is extremely important.

